 "post": {
  "title": "Your Favourite Letter Is Probably In Your Name #shorts",
  "description": "Was your letter in your name? Tell me in the comments. Send this to the friend whose favourite letter is their initial. Gus picks G because 'it just looks nice'. In 1985 the Belgian psychologist Jozef Nuttin (European Journal of Social Psychology) had people circle the letter they liked more in pairs of letters: they preferred letters from their own name more than other people did. In 1987 he repeated it across 12 European languages with over 2,000 students: the preference for one's own initials was clear in every language. Psychologists call it the name-letter effect. Not vanity: we just like what's ours. #psychology #shorts #nameletter #overthinking #funfacts",
